UPDATE 2026-09-05 (seat03): CLASSIFIED, confirmed, no new work needed. `large.icn` tests large-integer
arithmetic; first divergence line: SCRIP gives `9223372036854775807 + 9223372036854775807 = -2` (correct
64-bit two's-complement wraparound) where real icont/iconx gives `111111111111111111111 +
111111111111111111111 = 222222222222222222222` (arbitrary-precision bignum result -- verified directly
